{
  "contract": "routes.v1",
  "domain": "crm",
  "owner": "core/crm",
  "edge": "gateway",
  "note": "The optional CRM (ADR-0047). ABSENT unless the deployment names CRM_API_URL: then the edge fronts the verbs the terminal needs under /crm/* — the person's own Person and merge card (person/me, person/merge, person/profile: D35, a person's own credential only), the record page's read, history and review, and the desktop's desk/read, desk/arrange, desk/proposal and desk/undo, and the person's own workspace settings desk/workspaces/read and desk/workspaces/set (all served only while the `desktop` feature is on), and the cards' card/list, card/read, card/create, card/update, card/members and card/membership (served only while `desktop_cards` is on) —, forwarded onto crm-api's own paths, with the caller's key, which crm-api resolves through identity itself. Everything else about the CRM is the agent's: the crm_* tools in the one MCP. No row admits a worker's delegation token: the record page and the desktop are a person's, and review and applying a desktop suggestion take a person's own credential; workers reach the desk through the desktop_* tools and cards only through card_list / card_propose / card_update_propose (a proposed card is accepted through /crm/review, a person's).",
  "presence_env": "CRM_API_URL",
  "forward": {
    "edge_prefix": "/crm/",
    "upstream_prefix": "/"
  },
  "routes": [
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/crm/read",
      "scopes": [
        "bot",
        "tx"
      ],
      "shared": "allow"
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/crm/history",
      "scopes": [
        "bot",
        "tx"
      ],
      "shared": "refuse"
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/crm/review",
      "scopes": [
        "bot",
        "tx"
      ],
      "shared": "refuse"
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/crm/desk/read",
      "scopes": [
        "bot",
        "tx"
      ],
      "shared": "refuse"
    },
    {
      "method": "POST",
